============================
MP3
============================

--- prereqs ---

sudo apt install lame     # create mp3 files 
sudo apt install mpg123   # play mp3 file

--- create ---

lame -r -s 44.1 --bitwidth 16 --signed -m m captured_audio.pcm captured_audio.mp3
  -r raw
  -m m(ono)  s(tereo)

--- play ---

mpg123 captured_audio.mp3

--- lame recorder ---

source code
https://github.com/zlargon/lame/tree/master

license
Can I use LAME in my commercial program?  
Yes, you can, under the restrictions of the LGPL.  The easiest
way to do this is to:
1. Link to LAME as separate library (libmp3lame.a on unix or 
   lame_enc.dll or libmp3lame.dll on windows)
2. Fully acknowledge that you are using LAME, and give a link
   to our web site, www.mp3dev.org
3. If you make modifications to LAME, you *must* release these
   these modifications back to the LAME project, under the LGPL.

